{{also|stunde|stünde|stuņde}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|}}, from {{inh|de|goh|stunta}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*stundō||point in time, hour}}, from Proto-Indo-European *stut- (“prop”), from {{der|de|ine-pro|*steh₂-|t=to stand}}. Cognate with {{cog|hrx|Stunn}}, {{cog|nl|stond||time}}, {{cog|en|stound||hour, while}}, {{cog|da|stund||while}}, {{cog|no|stund||while}}, {{cog|se|stund||while}}. More at {{l|en|stound}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃtʊndə/}}
* {{a|Germany}} {{audio|de|De-Stunde.ogg}}
* {{a|Austria}} {{audio|de|De-at-Stunde.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f|dim=^chen,^lein}}

# [[hour]] {{gloss|unit of time consisting of 60 minutes}}
#: {{ux|de|Der Film dauert drei '''Stunden'''.|The movie lasts three '''hours.'''}}
# {{lb|de|dated}} [[hour]], [[moment]], [[time]] {{gloss|point in time}}
#: {{ux|de|Bitte für uns Sünder, jetzt und in der '''Stunde''' unsres Todes.|Pray for us sinners, now and at the '''hour''' of our death.}}
# [[lesson]]; [[class]] {{gloss|teaching unit, usually between 45 and 90 minutes}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich muss jetzt zur Klavier'''stunde.'''|I need to go to piano '''class''' right now.}}

